{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"harmonious-puzzling-chafer","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe store's event log grows without bound, so a periodic compaction pass must run on its own without anyone remembering to invoke it.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `.github/workflows/compact-store.yml`, a GitHub Actions workflow on a daily `schedule:` cron that checks out the tickets branch and runs `rebar compact`. The workflow is the trigger: nothing else invokes compaction.\n\n## Scope\n- `.github/workflows/compact-store.yml` — the new scheduled workflow.\n- `src/rebar/_store/compact.py` — the `rebar compact` entry point the workflow calls.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: a unit test asserts the workflow's `schedule:` cron is daily and its job runs `rebar compact`.\n- Edge: a test asserts compaction on an already-compact store is a no-op.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `.github/workflows/compact-store.yml` exists with a daily cron and runs `rebar compact`.\n- [ ] Compaction runs unattended once a day, verified by the workflow's run history.","id":"d67d-8167-86b5-446c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Scratch: scheduled store compaction"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786619751251989001,"uuid":"f548d660-4acf-4b7c-ba73-283f538dc2b3"}